# Example B1 with a pi+ beam and everything QBBC gives a pion that this port does not have,
# switched off. The P1 stage; see muon_emonly.mac beside it for why each line is here.
#
# `ref/oracle/species_processes.csv` for pi+: Transportation, msc (WentzelVIUni), hIoni
# (Bragg;BetheBloch, UrbanFluc), hBrems, hPairProd, CoulombScat, Decay, hadElastic, pi+Inelastic.
# The port has the first three.
#
#   hadElastic, pi+Inelastic   the hadronic processes. P5 and P9/P10/P11.
#   Decay                      a pi+ has a 26.033 ns proper lifetime. Over the 330 mm from B1's
#                              entrance face to the world boundary the pion falls from 200 to
#                              132 MeV, so mean gamma is about 2.19 and mean beta about 0.89:
#                              a lab lifetime of 57.0 ns against a flight time of 1.24 ns, and
#                              1 - exp(-1.24/57.0) = 2.1% of them decay IN FLIGHT. This port
#                              does not decay one at all. P4.
#                              CORRECTED: this read "what decays is the STOPPED pion - which is
#                              most of them, at the end of the track", which requires the pion
#                              to stop in B1 and it does not (see the range below).
#   hBrems, hPairProd          discrete radiative, unported final states. Pair production does
#                              not start until max(850 MeV, 8*139.57) = 1.12 GeV, and the brem
#                              mean free path at 200 MeV in water is 1.8e6 mm, so this pair of
#                              lines should be worth nothing here. docs/RISK.md V38.
#   CoulombScat                unported; P14.
#
# 200 MeV pi+: 782.2 mm of water (ref/oracle/hadron_tables.csv, G4_WATER at 199.5262 MeV), so
# it CROSSES B1's 300 mm envelope and exits at about 132 MeV. CORRECTED: this line read "about
# 25 cm of water, so it stops inside B1's envelope", wrong by a factor of three and wrong about
# the fate; see muon_emonly.mac for why the distinction is load-bearing.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 0

/process/inactivate hadElastic
/process/inactivate pi+Inelastic
/process/inactivate Decay
/process/inactivate hBrems
/process/inactivate hPairProd
/process/inactivate CoulombScat

/gun/particle pi+
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 2000
/run/beamOn 10000
